    <!-- Tutorial -->
    <string name="tutorial_title">How to Play</string>
    <string name="tutorial_basics_title">The Basics</string>
    <string name="tutorial_basics_body">Japanese words fall from the top of the screen, showing their kanji. Type the word\'s reading before it reaches the line at the bottom.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_typing_title">Typing</string>
    <string name="tutorial_typing_body">As you type, your input is shown converted to kana. Any word on screen whose reading matches gets highlighted — finish it exactly and it clears automatically, no tapping needed.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_spelling_title">Tricky Spellings</string>
    <string name="tutorial_spelling_body">Long vowels are typed literally: とうきょう is toukyou, not tokyo. Type ん as nn, and a small っ by doubling the next consonant (きって = kitte). For the katakana long mark (ー) you can type a dash or spell out the vowel.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_dead_input_title">Watch for Red</string>
    <string name="tutorial_dead_input_body">If your input doesn\'t match the start of any word on screen, it turns red. Backspace and try again.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_misses_title">Misses &amp; Lives</string>
    <string name="tutorial_misses_body">A word that reaches the line costs a life and briefly flashes its reading. You start with 3 lives — lose them all and the run ends.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_scoring_title">Combo &amp; Scoring</string>
    <string name="tutorial_scoring_body">Clearing words quickly and back-to-back builds a combo for bonus points. Longer words and harder kanji are worth more.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_furigana_title">Furigana</string>
    <string name="tutorial_furigana_body">Turn on furigana in Settings to show each word\'s reading above it — helpful while you\'re still learning.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_input_mode_title">Input Modes</string>
    <string name="tutorial_input_mode_body">By default you type romaji (Latin letters), automatically converted to kana. In Settings you can switch to typing hiragana directly with a Japanese keyboard instead.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_modes_title">Game Modes</string>
    <string name="tutorial_modes_body">Endless: pick a difficulty and play until you run out of lives. Campaign: clear structured levels — reach the target number of clears to pass and unlock the next one. After passing you can keep playing to push your score higher.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_pause_title">Pausing</string>
    <string name="tutorial_pause_body">Tap the pause button anytime. The game also pauses automatically if you leave the app mid-run.</string>
